1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,640
The loneliest sentence Jesus ever spoke wasn't

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:03,260
his own line.

3
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:07,300
He was quoting, Psalm 22 opens in the voice

4
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,360
of a forsaken man.

5
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:12,100
David wrote it, Jesus made it his own.

6
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:17,380
David's very first line, my God, my God, why

7
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:19,000
hast thou forsaken me?

8
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:21,740
A thousand years later, at the ninth hour,

9
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:23,620
Jesus cried it from the cross.

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:28,180
My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?

11
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:29,680
The very same words.

12
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:32,720
This was no cry of lost faith.

13
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:37,200
Even forsaken, he still calls God, my God.

14
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:41,420
It was the sinless Son taking our place and

15
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:43,720
bearing the forsaking that our sin deserved.

16
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:47,800
He was forsaken so that you never will be.

17
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:51,800
However far you've run, the way home is open,

18
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,700
and he opened it from the dark.
